  "family": "classical",
  "lineage": "Court music of the Mossi kingdoms of Burkina Faso, centred on the palace of the Moogo Naaba in Ouagadougou. Hereditary court drummers led by the bendr-naaba recite royal genealogies and histories on the bendré, a large calabash drum with a skin head, alongside lunga hourglass talking drums and praise singing at palace ceremonies. The bara card stands in for the bendré and the talking-drum card for the lunga.",
